SUMMARY:North Humber River Long Walk  - 16KM (You might see a deer!)
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n### 🌿 North Humber River Walk 
 – 6th Annual! 🌿\n\nWe’re back for our **sixth year in a row** with 
 this incredible walk — and it has become a true fan favourite!\nThe Nort
 h Humber River trail is one of Toronto’s most peaceful and nature-filled
  walks. It’s a longer walk\, but that’s part of what makes it so rewar
 ding.\n\nYou’ll get out of the city\, follow the river\, explore beautif
 ul natural areas\, and see just how far you can go when you give yourself 
 the chance.\n\nThis walk is about challenging yourself just a little — y
 ou'd be surprised how far you can go!\nIf you don't want to complete the e
 ntire walk\, that's totally okay. You can leave along the way\, and I can 
 help you find the nearest way back toward public transit.\nWe'll finish wi
 th a quick stop at Tim Hortons before heading back toward Kipling Station.
 \n\n### 📲 Stay Connected\n\nDon't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group 
 – [CLICK HERE!](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\nIt'
 s a great way to get updates\, connect with other members\, and stay infor
 med about the event.\n\n***\n\n###\n\n***\n\n### 📍 Meetup Details\n\n
 🕙 **Meetup Time:** 10:00 AM\n🚌 **Bus leaves:** 10:06 AM sharp\n📍 
 **Meetup Spot:** In front of the Information Booth at Kipling Subway Stati
 on Bus Terminal\n🫎 Look for Mathew in the Moose Hat!\n🚌 **Bus:** 927
 B Highway 27 Express to Steeles via Humber College\n\n⚠️ **PLEASE BE O
 N TIME.**\nIf you miss the bus\, you will miss the group. We cannot wait f
 or late arrivals.\n\n***\n\n### 🚗 Driving / Meeting Us at the Trail\n\n
 If you live closer to the trail or prefer to drive\, **you can meet us at 
 Humberline Park**.\n📍 **Meeting Point:** Humberline Park\, by the bathr
 ooms\n⏰ **Meeting Time:** Approximately **10:35 AM**\n\nPlease look up d
 irections to Humberline Park before leaving and give yourself plenty of ti
 me to get there.\n🚗 **Parking:** Parking availability in the area can v
 ary\, so please check the parking situation before coming.\n\n⚠️ **Imp
 ortant:** If you drive to Humberline Park\, **you will need to arrange you
 r own transportation back at the end of the walk.**\n\nWe do not finish th
 e walk back at Humberline Park. You may need to use Uber\, a taxi\, or pub
 lic transit to get back to your vehicle.\nIf you're meeting us at the park
 \, please make sure you are there and ready to walk by 10:35 AM. Once we a
 rrive\, we'll be continuing with the group.\n\n***\n\n### 💵 Meetup Fee\
 n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com]
 (mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n\nThis small fee helps support the g
 roup and keeps events like this running. Thank you for supporting the comm
 unity!\n\n***\n\n### 🌲 What to Expect\n\n🚍 A 40-minute bus ride to t
 he starting point near Humber College\n🌿 A peaceful walk along the Nort
 h Humber River\n🦌 Opportunities to spot deer\, birds\, and other wildli
 fe\n☕ Two rest stops along the route\n🥾 A longer walk that will give 
 you a chance to challenge yourself\n🍩 A final stop at Tim Hortons befor
 e heading back toward Kipling Station\n\nSome sections of this trail genui
 nely feel like you've left Toronto behind. It's one of those walks where t
 he city slowly disappears and you're surrounded by trees\, water\, wildlif
 e\, and open space.\n\n***\n\n### 🧳 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 G
 ood walking shoes — some sections may be uneven\n🥨 A snack\n🧴 Suns
 creen\n🎒 A small backpack\n\n***\n\n### 👥 Who Is This For?\n\nThis g
 roup is for anyone who wants to get outside\, explore Toronto\, and meet p
 eople along the way — singles\, couples\, newcomers\, longtime Torontoni
 ans\, and everyone in between.\n\nWe host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hike
 s\n🎭 Arts & culture\n🍽️ Restaurants\n🎤 Karaoke\n…and plenty m
 ore!\n\nThe activity is the **container**. The people you meet and the con
 nections you make along the way are the real experience. 💛\n\n***\n\n##
 # 💛 A Few Notes\n\nYou're welcome to join us even if you're deciding at
  the last minute.\nIf you need to leave the walk early\, that's okay — j
 ust let me know and we'll help you figure out the best way to get back tow
 ard transit.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled 
 or changed. Please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n***\n\n
 👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n📧 Questions? Post on the event wall or emai
 l:\n**[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings
 @hotmail.com)**
