SUMMARY:Sunday Leisure Walk (BuskerFest Festival—Walk\, Talk and Have Fu
 n!)
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nHello everyone\,\n\n\\*Please read
  carefully\\*\n\nGet ready for an afternoon filled with laughter\, amazing
  street performances and new friendships at the Toronto International Busk
 erFest! We’ll walk through the festival together\, enjoy the sights and 
 sounds\, and take in some of the most creative and entertaining performers
  Toronto has to offer.\n\\*Many of us will probably head down to the Beach
 es Boardwalk and/or Queen Street too for more site seeing\, ice cream and 
 find a nice place for dinner and beverages after\n\n\\*Joined by my other 
 groups too :)\n\n**Arrive between 4:00 pm and 4:30 pm**\n\n**Where to meet
  us:**\n\nMeetup us outside **Woodbine Station beside bike racks**\n**The 
 Main Woodbine Station Entrance:** Located at the southeast corner of Woodb
 ine Avenue and Strathmore Boulevard.\n\nWe will walk as a group from the s
 tation down to Ashbridges Bay\n\\*Most will stick around after for a bite 
 to eat and a beverage to sip on :)\n\nFurther details below:\n\nSincerely\
 ,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\n**Event Details:**\n**Sunday Leis
 ure Walk (The Toronto International BuskerFest Festival—Walk\, Talk and 
 Have Fun!)**\n\nWhat to expect:\n\n* A relaxed walk together along Woodbin
 e to the BuskerFest Festival\n* Ice breaker games to get to know one anoth
 er\n* Plenty of opportunities to mix\, mingle and meet new people\n* A com
 fortable pace that allows everyone to walk and talk\n* Beautiful views of 
 the lake\, beach\, parkland and surrounding area during and after BuskerFe
 st\n* A positive atmosphere for both newcomers and returning members\n\nPl
 ease wear comfortable walking shoes and bring water\, sunscreen or anythin
 g else you may need for the weather. The purpose of this event is simple: 
 get outside\, enjoy the day and make a few new connections!\n\n{Optional R
 ead: **More about BuskerFest}**\nFrom musicians and jugglers to acrobats\,
  comedians and living statues\, BuskerFest offers something unexpected aro
 und every corner. This outing is a wonderful opportunity to explore the fe
 stival at a relaxed pace while talking\, laughing and connecting with othe
 r friendly folks. Come by yourself or bring a friend—our focus is simply
  to have fun\, enjoy the performances\, see other parts the water front an
 d make everyone feel welcome.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Event Fee:**\n10 dollars (cash only) w
 hen you arrive (HST is included)\nor e transfer in advance to [Steveflemmi
 ng11@gmail.com](mailto:Steveflemming11@gmail.com)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n(Optio
 nal to support the festival once we arrive-extra cost:\n**Admission**: **B
 y donation** at the gate (a suggested donation of $5 to $10 per person ben
 efiting [Epilepsy Toronto](https://epilepsytoronto.org/about-us/events/tor
 onto-international-buskerfest-for-epilepsy/). Tip your street performers s
 eparately if you enjoy their acts!\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\nParking near Woodbine Station:\n(Althou
 gh I encourage you to take subway if you can)
